For every fold \(\ell\) and \(u\in\{0,1,2\}\), conditional on its training complement, bounded outcomes, clipped nuisances, overlap, bounded features, and compact \(\Theta\) give \(\|F_{\ell,u}\|_{P,2}\le C_{\mathrm{sm}}(r_{m,n}+r_{e,n})\) and \(\sup_{
u}\log N(\varepsilon\|F_{\ell,u}\|_{
u,2},\mathcal F_{\ell,u},L^2(
u))\le C_{\mathrm{sm}}d\log(C_{\mathrm{sm}}/\varepsilon)\) for \(0<\varepsilon\le1\), where the supremum is over the declared finitely supported laws \(
u\). For the composed estimated-influence replacement path, \(\Lambda_n=O_{\mathbb P}(1)\), so \(\log\mathsf N_n(\varepsilon)\le\log\{1+\Lambda_n\operatorname{diam}(\mathcal C)/\varepsilon\}\) on events whose probability tends to one. Moreover, conditionally on the data, \(E_\xi[\sup_{c\in\mathcal C}\|n^{-1/2}\sum_{i=1}^n\xi_i\Delta_i(c)\|\mid O_1,\ldots,O_n]\le C_{\mathrm{sm}}\delta_n\sqrt{1+\log\{1+\Lambda_n\operatorname{diam}(\mathcal C)/\delta_n\}}\), with the right side defined as zero when \(\delta_n=0\). Thus \(\delta_n=o_{\mathbb P}(1)\) is sufficient for conditional multiplier replacement.
